  "notes": "ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-003 (curl-reproducible exploit probe) does not apply: this chunk is skill-authoring documentation/workflow prose, not a running service — there is no endpoint to curl. security-BLK-1 is a design-level authorization-bypass finding in the smine proposal-apply pipeline (smine-skills + smine-apply + smine-orchestrate), demonstrated by citing the exact prose that creates the gap, not by a live request. Cross-chunk note for the station: the casual-lockout gate's only other enforcement point is smine-orchestrate/SKILL.md (not in this chunk's file list, but read as context) — its step 1 re-checks the same origin:user marker and would also pass an auto-stamped new skill, so the gap is not caught downstream either; this is reported here since smine-orchestrate is out of my assigned chunk.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "security-BLK-1",
      "file": "skills/smine/smine-skills/SKILL.md",
