      "checklist": "ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-001",
      "claim": "The casual-lockout control — meant to stop unreviewed skill content from reaching a casual-audience install — only gates EDITS to existing skills; creation of a brand-new skill is explicitly exempted and smine-apply auto-stamps every new skill it creates with the exact `origin: user` marker the lockout keys on. In `always` (or an under-specified `decide`) auto-apply mode, this lets a skill candidate mined out of ordinary session transcripts — with no human vote — become a fully trusted, lockout-exempt skill in one nightly run, and SKILL.md prose is instructions a future agent session follows, not inert data.",
      "fix": "Make new-skill creation subject to the same casual-lockout gate as edits (hold `casual-locked` / require an explicit human `+` vote, never an auto-apply candidate, when audience is casual), and/or never auto-stamp `origin: user` on anything the pipeline itself created — reserve that marker for skills a human actually authored or explicitly voted `+` on by id.",
      "evidence": "Re-read skills/smine/smine-skills/SKILL.md:45 (committed e5245d08d2fe5c05f67742fd8ec5a67b759ca316): \"Casual lockout — ... an edit (skill or workflow) may target only a skill whose SKILL.md frontmatter carries origin: user. ... New-skill proposals stay allowed — smine-apply stamps them origin: user at creation.\" Cross-checked against skills/smine/smine-apply/SKILL.md:31: \"a new skill created from a proposal additionally gets origin: user in its frontmatter ..., the provenance marker the casual lockout keys on (never added to shipped skills, never removed)\" and step 5 (Auto-apply): in `always` mode every remaining `proposed` skills-kind entry becomes an implicit `+` vote up to the implementation cap, with no rules-file judgment required (that gate is `decide`-mode only, and even there judges against a user-authored rules file, not against injection risk). smine-batch/SKILL.md (mining source, read in full) confirms session transcripts — including pasted external content — are mined verbatim into skill-candidate findings with no sanitization beyond quoting; smine-skills/SKILL.md step 1 turns such a candidate into a `skills.json` proposal, and smine-apply's step 4 skills route then has an agent author the actual SKILL.md body from that proposal and stamp it origin: user, unconditionally. No known-findings or rejected-findings entry covers this path (checked round-2/known.json and rejected.json, both lack any smine-skills/smine-apply origin:user entry). The claim survives re-check: the exemption is explicit in both files' prose, not an inference."
    }
  ],
